form.section:
Unless Additional Terms amend this allocation: Seller pays internal-revenue
stamps on the original deed and the cost of cancelling Seller liens;
Buyer pays stamps on the certified copy and Registro presentation fees;
the notarial tariff on the sale deed is allocated as the Parties agree in
Additional Terms (and otherwise as the Notary invoices inside the legal
band); title study and commitment are Seller's cost; a lender's policy,
bank fees, appraisal, new survey, and inspections are Buyer's cost; HOA
documents and estoppel are Seller's cost; each Party pays its own counsel;
broker commissions are paid under separate listing or buyer-representation
agreements, not as a condition of the validity of this sale.
